@verbs build ring builder-ring
@tier coder
@title the builder ring: the verb that makes a world
@see update cd

  build <what> ...

Everything about converting rooms into locations, laying out an
area, its points of interest, its jobs, its houses and its families
is one verb, and the verb lives on the builder ring you carry.

The ring has to be worn first: 'equip' puts it on, and until then
'build' only says so.

The ring documents itself, and its list is the one that matches the
code you are running:

  build                 lists every form of the verb.
  help ring             the same list, with what the ring is for.

That list is not repeated here because it grows with the builder.
